NAME
    finder - the full-screen desktop / file browser (graphics mode)

SYNOPSIS
    finder

DESCRIPTION
    The Mac-style desktop for the graphics display (two-mode P4). One
    program owns the whole screen -- no tiling, no overlapping windows.
    A white menu bar runs across the top showing the current directory;
    the rest of the screen is that directory as a scrolling file list.

    Requires a display (a GL card fitted, GFXPRES=1); on a headless
    machine it prints "?No display" and exits. Finder claims the screen
    (it suspends the on-screen text console while it runs) and draws its
    own UI with the card's stroke font.

KEYS
    Up / Down  (or k / j)   move the selection
    ENTER                   open the selection:
                              a directory  -> navigate INTO it
                              a .BIN        -> LAUNCH it full-screen
                                               (this program BECOMES the app)
    Backspace / Left        go up one directory
    q  or  ESC              quit the desktop -> back to the command line

    Directories show in cyan with a leading "/"; the selected row is a
    yellow bar.

NOTES
    Launching an app is a full-screen program swap (SYS_EXEC). Automatic
    return to the desktop when the app quits (the -d/-w resume chain), an
    Apps menu, mouse support, and the file operations (rename, duplicate,
    move) are not yet wired -- see the project backlog. Grows out of the
    older tiled `desk`, made full-screen.

SEE ALSO
    desk, paint, screen
